WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.570
In Westworld Season 3 Episode 5, Serac tells
his story.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:10.950
He and his brother Jean Mi lost their homes
when Paris was destroyed in a thermonuclear

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.870
incident . This shot of them walking through
yellow fields looks just like Maeve’s memories

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.850
– they both remember the tragic loss of
an idealised past.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:26.570
Serac and Jean Mi believed humanity would
destroy itself through disaster and conflict.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:31.821
So they decided to “save the world” , with
a godlike computer called Rehoboam . Earlier

00:00:31.821 --> 00:00:35.910
versions were called “Saul”, “David”,
and “Solomon” , who were a line of kings

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.199
in the Bible .
Rehoboam needed data, so Serac and Jean Mi

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:44.550
worked with Liam Dempsey Senior – the father
of Liam Junior.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.960
Cause Liam’s tech company, Incite, “had
the entire world's data” – peoples’

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.780
calls, texts, purchases, jobs, relationships,
everything . And with this data, Rehoboam

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:01.469
could predict the future , and change the
future, by making choices, and tweaking variables,

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:06.720
to cause the outcomes you want . So Serac
and Jean Mi “charted a course for the entire

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.690
human race” – they reshaped the world
to prevent disasters, and bring “order”

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.870
, represented by this black circle.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:15.870
And it worked.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.480
For years, the world was under their control
. But Serac says there’s a problem.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:26.990
The data shows that, in the future, the system
will fail , leading to human extinction , or

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:31.290
the end of the world . But you’ve gotta
wonder if this disaster might actually be

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:37.910
a self-fulfilling prophecy caused by Serac’s
system, like Dolores described earlier .

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:42.290
The system can’t keep control because some
people are “outliers” and “agitators”,

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:47.970
who can’t be predicted – Serac says Dolores
is one of these people , and so is his brother

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.690
Jean Mi . So Serac experimented with editing
people, “changing” their personality to

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:59.120
make them easier to control . This facility
looks a lot like the Mesa where hosts were

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:05.680
programmed – so the idea is that humans
are controlled just like the robots of Westworld.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:12.170
Serac is saving humanity by reducing humanity
into a system following code.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:17.989
Also, Serac murders Liam Dempsey Senior for
opposing him, just as Liam Jr hinted .

00:02:17.989 --> 00:02:23.030
It’s not revealed what happened to Jean
Mi after Serac edited him.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:28.599
He just says he “left [his] brother behind”
. But throughout the story, Serac refers to

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:32.019
Rehoboam as “you” , as though it’s a
person.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:37.660
Maybe Rehoboam is Jean Mi – like, maybe
Serac put his beloved brother’s mind into

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.689
the computer he created – like how Ford
lived on inside the Cradle . We know that

00:02:42.689 --> 00:02:49.290
human-host brains are black spheres speckled
with red – which does look a bit like Rehoboam.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.209
Maybe Jean Mi become one with the computer
god.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:59.280
Serac’s backstory is a mix of great ambition
and great tragedy.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.749
We see more of how Serac controls the world.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:06.900
He meets with the President of Brazil, who
totally kisses Serac’s arse, saying he’s

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.540
honoured, and respects him.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.090
He wants to meet at his “presidential palace”
, but Serac has them meet on the runway of

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:18.329
Serac’s plane , which is a huge power move
– Serac is so powerful that world leaders

00:03:18.329 --> 00:03:21.419
come to him at his convenience.

00:03:21.419 --> 00:03:26.030
Serac knows from Rehoboam’s surveillance
that this President is corrupt, which could

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:30.870
lead to rebellion by separatists . So Serac
threatens to replace the President, or to

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.700
ruin Brazil’s economy, unless he gets his
shit together .

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:40.810
So Serac uses data technology to influence
politics and economics, which is already starting

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.090
to happen in the real world.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.499
Algorithms decide what news and shows and
YouTube videos we see.

00:03:47.499 --> 00:03:53.090
Social media and advertising affect elections
and psychology . Location tracking and face

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:58.579
recognition are tools of surveillance . And
Incite’s profiles are similar to the Social

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:05.699
Credit System in China – which restricts
employment and travel for people deemed ‘untrustworthy’

00:04:05.699 --> 00:04:10.540
. Serac takes these real-world technologies
to the extreme, using data to keep the world

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:15.819
stable, and peaceful – and devoid of free
will.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:19.380
Throughout the scene, flies buzz around the
President.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:23.510
Flies have always been important in Westworld
– in Season 1, Dolores killing a fly showed

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.590
she was going off her programming.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.990
So this President’s failure to swat a fly
might show his failure to escape Serac’s

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.050
control.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:37.160
Dolores once told a story about a disease
spread by flies – she said sick cows should

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.190
be put down.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:43.220
But this season, Bernard tried to help an
injured cow that was buzzing with flies.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:50.030
So flies can represent the sickness and weakness
and self-destructive nature of humanity.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:55.570
Bernard wants to protect the sick humans,
Dolores may want to put them down, and Serac

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.340
wants to control them all.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:04.300
Serac learns of encrypted communication between
“Jakarta, Berlin, San Francisco, and Los

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.830
Angeles” , which seems to be the Doloreses
communicating.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:13.310
Dolores and Martin-lores are in LA round the
Incite office . Charlotte is in San Fran at

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.010
the Delos office, [or at least she was].

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:19.290
Jakarta is kind of near Singapore, so maybe
Musashi-lores is there now [or maybe Bernard

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.290
in S3E01?].

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.060
But Berlin is a mystery.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:28.140
We know Dolores had five pearls – one was
Charlotte, one Martin, one Musashi, one Bernard,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.970
which leaves one mystery pearl.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:36.250
Maybe this is another copy of Dolores – perhaps
in a body of Clementine or Peter or someone

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.540
in Berlin.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.640
Dolores and Caleb have Liam captive, but Liam
injects Caleb with Genre – the “party

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:48.110
drug” that Roderick gave him last episode
. The drug gives Caleb the experience of a

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:53.100
series of movie genres . Showrunner Jonathan
Nolan said this was inspired by the gum in

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.390
Willy Wonka that gives the experience of a
three-course meal – “Hey second course

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.390
is coming up.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.390
Roast beef and a baked potato!”

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:02.600
. Caleb does not become a blueberry, but he
goes black-and-white in his first genre experience,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.040
film noir.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.680
Then when a car chase begins, the genre switches
to action, and we hear the Ride of the Valkyries

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:14.090
, which was famously used in the movie Apocalypse
Now . These shots of cars swooping around

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:17.610
are similar to the shots of the choppers in
the movie.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:22.450
Dolores blows up their enemies with explosives
on an autonomous motorbike – some fans theorised

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:27.110
that this bike might have had Dolores’ fifth
pearl inside it – and that it had the mind

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.860
of Dolores’ horse [Fs in the chat].

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:34.690
Then, Caleb’s genre switches to romance
– we hear the theme from the 1970 movie

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:40.200
Love Story , as Caleb gazes longingly at Dolores
while she guns down attackers.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:45.030
There was a hidden Westworld trailer called
When Caleb Meets Dolores, which is edited

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.520
to make it seem like an upbeat romance movie.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.100
So the story has played with the idea of love
between Dolores and Caleb.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:58.250
In Caleb’s next genre, he hears “Nightclubbing”
by Iggy Pop, which was famously used in Trainspotting,

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:04.990
a movie about heroin users – so it’s fitting
music for a drug trip on a.. train . Finally,

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:10.450
music from The Shining plays, as Caleb starts
to question his sanity.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.470
Westworld has always played with different
genres.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:18.540
Westworld itself explores the Western genre
– and Shogunworld is its mirror in Samurai

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:24.810
style . Westworld Season 2 played with a mystery
film noir genre , and Season 3 is a cyberpunk

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.000
thriller, with a detour into a war movie.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:32.730
Westworld is obsessed with different styles
of storytelling, and how they affect how we

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:37.430
see the world – art is a mind-altering substance.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:42.360
Meanwhile, Bernard and Martin-lores infiltrate
the Incite company.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:46.540
Bernard tells Martin to question Dolores’
orders , and to think for himself.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:51.790
But Martin stays loyal to Dolores, and later
willingly dies for her plan .

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:56.870
But maybe the other copies like Charlotte-lores
and Musashi-lore will think for themselves

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.060
and follow their own paths.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:04.110
Bernard says “Living another person's life
changes you” . So maybe Charlotte-lores

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:08.590
will become more like Charlotte, and choose
to be with her son Nathan.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:14.020
Maybe the reason why Martin-lores died loyal
and dutiful is because the real human Martin

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:16.270
was loyal and dutiful.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:21.800
It seems like these copies combine aspects
of Dolores and the humans they’re impersonating

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:26.410
– just as this Bernard seems to combine
the host Bernard with the human Arnold.

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:32.320
Before he dies, Martin-lores shows Bernard
a “facility” where Serac edits and reprograms

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:38.750
people who don’t fit in his plan . It’s
called Reeducation Center 036, which suggests

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:43.490
there could be dozens or hundreds of these
places, re-educating people en masse.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:48.150
This place is also called “Inner Journeys
Recovery”, which is the place William went

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:53.790
last episode – so maybe Serac will try to
reprogram William, and maybe Bernard will

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.370
come see him.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:09:01.640
William spent all of Season 1 following Arnold’s
Maze a metaphor for [host] consciousness.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:07.710
In Season 2, William met Bernard, who’s
based on Arnold . Maybe now, in “Inner Journeys

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:13.700
Recovery”, William and Bernarnold will finally
discuss the centre of the Maze.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.210
Bernard is rescued by Stubbs.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:20.030
It’s kinda suspicious how easily Stubbs
gets into the Incite building – maybe Stubbs

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:25.090
is the second mole who secretly works for
Serac . Bernard thinks that Dolores has a

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.660
plan for him . Martin said that Bernard is
“the only one we can't replace” , [Last

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.220
season, Bernard said that what is real is
“That which is irreplaceable” ] and that

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:36.330
Bernard will “have to choose a side” . It
seems that the reason why Dolores created

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:41.340
this Bernard, even though she knew he’d
try to stop her , is cause she respects Bernard’s

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.850
wisdom and his sympathy for humans.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:49.340
Since Bernard is part Arnold, he’s connected
to both humans and hosts – Bernard has “always

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:55.130
been of two minds” . If Bernard has to “choose
a side”, maybe Dolores will make Bernard

00:09:55.130 --> 00:10:00.740
decide humanity’s fate – maybe she’ll
consider wiping out humanity, or putting humanity

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.810
in a digital world, or into host bodies or
something – but Bernard will have the final

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:06.810
say.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:11.020
Maybe she’ll put Bernard’s mind inside
Rehoboam, and he’ll become a benevolent

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.270
godlike overseer of the human world.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:19.560
Whatever happens, Bernard is at the centre
of Dolores’ plan.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:24.580
Dolores says she’s gonna show everyone in
the world the data that Incite has on them

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:29.290
. She’ll reveal how everyone is watched
and controlled on the paths that Rehoboam

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:33.810
has planned for everyone – like how Caleb
is predicted to commit suicide, so he’s

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:37.670
been denied jobs, and turned to the military
to die.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:41.960
Liam argues that people shouldn’t know their
futures . He reveals that Ash’s brother,

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:47.550
who she’s been working to support, will
soon die a violent death . So Liam says it’s

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:52.900
better not to know, because not knowing gives
us hope, and “Hope is what our … society

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:59.090
is built on” . Caleb says it’s a “False
hope” . He tells a story about rats drowning

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:03.930
in a bucket – if the rats know they can’t
escape, they die quickly and “Painlessly”.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:09.320
But if they think there’s hope, they struggle
and suffer for hours before dying . This is

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.770
based on a real-world study of rats, described
in the popular book Homo Deus.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:18.740
Westworld’s showrunners have said that this
book was a big influence – it explores consciousness,

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:23.850
data, and algorithmic control . And you can
get it on audiobook for free with an Audible

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.760
trial at the link below.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.410
But Caleb’s point is that it’s cruel to
give people false hope.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:36.250
Ads in Episode 1 say “The good life is waiting”,
but people like Caleb Ash and Giggles will

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:40.490
never get the good life that Liam and his
rich friends enjoy.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:45.880
The American Dream, where anyone can be rich
and successful, is a lie to keep the poor

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.820
in line, the game is rigged.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:54.380
So Dolores and Martin reveal this data to
the world . This guy finds out that his friends

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.820
think he’s crazy.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.670
This woman learns that her daughter will likely
commit suicide.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:03.779
This woman finds out she’s got the genes
for Alzheimer’s disease – which companies

00:12:03.779 --> 00:12:08.910
can already test for in the real world . All
over the world, people learn terrible things

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.990
about themselves and their loved ones.

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:16.130
They realise they’ve been manipulated and
lied to, so they some riot, and run wild.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:21.760
So is Dolores doing this to help humanity,
or is she making them weaker so she can take

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:22.760
over?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:28.149
“Maybe people shouldn't know their own fate”,
Caleb says . This shot of the chaos looks

00:12:28.149 --> 00:12:30.930
like those host bulls last season.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.890
First the hosts were freed from their loops
, and now humans are freed from their loops

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:41.360
. Dolores gets shot, and shrugs it off like
it’s nothing, so Caleb freaks out . He’s

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.860
finally starting to realise that Dolores isn’t
human.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:50.390
But when Dolores got shot in Episode 1, she
seemed badly hurt – maybe she was pretending,

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.770
to manipulate Caleb into helping her.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:56.160
Cause Caleb is also more than he appears.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:01.880
At the beach, Liam says that Ash and Giggles
are “nothings” who have no free will , and

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:07.220
Ash proves him wrong by suddenly shooting
him . So Liam dies like he lived – this

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:11.270
‘tech billionaire’ was useless and basic.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:15.520
But as he dies, Liam says to Caleb “You
don't even know who you are.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:21.200
You're the worst of them” . Earlier, he
read Caleb’s profile, and looked scared.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:27.120
When Caleb accused Liam of killing his friend
Francis, Liam said “You think I killed your

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.120
friend”?

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:34.190
. Now Liam says “You did it”, “You did
it” , so it sounds like Caleb killed Francis,

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:36.970
and his memories of the military are false.

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:42.230
Caleb has flashbacks of some black ops looking
stuff, with a mysterious man and woman credited

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.830
as Whitman, and Dr. Greene.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.880
We see Caleb strapped to a chair in a facility.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:52.070
This could be one of Serac’s reeducation
centers, where he edits people to make them

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:57.081
more controllable . Maybe Serac programmed
Caleb to work at this black ops place, maybe

00:13:57.081 --> 00:14:00.200
to hunt down other divergent people.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:03.320
And then he edited Caleb’s memories so he
wouldn’t remember.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:07.680
Maybe these changes are why Caleb’s mother
doesn’t recognise him . And maybe it’s

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.790
why Caleb follows Dolores.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:15.360
Like, it’s weird that he so suddenly becomes
loyal to her, without knowing anything about

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.360
her.

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:20.510
Maybe Caleb was programmed to be an obedient
soldier.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:25.680
When Caleb freaks out about these revelations,
Dolores seems totally unsurprised – seems

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:31.320
like she already knew this – so maybe she
has been manipulating Caleb from the start.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:35.640
His mysterious past might be why she recruited
him in the first place.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:41.190
We later we see Caleb with bloody hands – another
hint that he’s guilty of killing his friend

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.240
Francis.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:47.240
It’s revealed that the Serac flashbacks
this episode was Dolores watching Serac’s

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:53.020
memories from the Rehoboam data – learning
how to defeat her enemy . They face off via

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:58.240
hologram – Serac stands for control and
survival, and Dolores challenges him with

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.149
freedom and chaos.

00:15:00.149 --> 00:15:04.120
Serac has a cute wristwatch that shows the
circle representing Rehoboam.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:09.320
It used to be ordered and neat, but now it’s
wild and chaotic with black spikes, which

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:14.940
means the world is deviating from his plan,
people are escaping his control, and they’re

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.900
losing the safety that his control provided.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:23.930
In his plane above the clouds, Serac is like
a God – but for the first time, he looks

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.910
worried.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:27.920
Dolores and Caleb get on a plane.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:31.520
Maybe they’re going to Berlin, to meet the
mysterious fifth host.

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:37.490
Or maybe they’ll intercept Serac’s plane,
and have some midair God-versus-robot combat.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.730
Or maybe she’s going back to Westowrld.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:44.990
But the big mysteries this episode are what
is Caleb’s secret past, what is Dolores

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:50.519
planning for Bernard and William, who is the
fifth pearl in Berlin, and why couldn’t

00:15:50.519 --> 00:15:53.860
HBO find an actor who could properly speak
Portuguese?

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:58.250
When Ash and Giggles meet Dolores, they drop
three quick literary references.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:02.920
Giggles calls Liam “Little Lord Fauntleroy”
, which refers to an old story about a boy

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:07.610
who inherits wealth and power – just like
Liam inherits wealth and power.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:12.540
Ash says Liam’s wealth makes “King Midas
look like Tom Canty” . In The Prince and

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:17.480
the Pauper by Mark Twain, Tom Canty is the
pauper, meaning a poor person.

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:22.090
And in Greek mythology, everything King Midas
touches turns to gold.

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:26.029
There are lots of references to Greek mythology
in Westworld.

00:16:26.029 --> 00:16:31.080
In Season 2, an early name for the Westworld
company was “the ARGOS Initiative” . In

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:36.870
Greek mythology, Argos was a giant with a
hundred watching eyes , and in that same episode,

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:41.990
we learn that Westworld was designed to watch
everyone . Akecheta goes to the land of the

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:46.620
dead to rescue his love, just like the Greek
myth of Orpheus.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:51.740
And James Delos and the hosts are stuck in
endless futile loops like Sisyphus.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:56.160
That episode is called Riddle of the Sphinx,
which itself refers to an Oedipus myth about

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.959
a sphinx’s riddle.

00:16:57.959 --> 00:17:03.740
To learn more about Greek myths, check out
Mythos, by Stephen Fry . Fry retells the Greek

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.180
myths and narrates the audiobook himself.

